The copy constructor is already a trivial member-wise copy; the only safe micro-optimisation is to let the compiler emit the minimal copy sequence by keeping the initializer list in declaration order (avoiding any reordering overhead) and copying nothing extra.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```